{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.no_bondFunctional_of_b3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.no_bondFunctional_of_b3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L194-L201","doc":"Contrapositive, stated so a reader holding the measurement can apply it\ndirectly: a nonzero connected three-body cumulant excludes **every** bond\nfunctional at once, rather than excluding them one at a time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3_eq_zero_ofBondFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3_eq_zero_ofBondFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L186-L192","doc":"**The conclusion of the file.** Whatever bond functional §10a's Cauchy\nargument selects — the forced logarithm included — the induced binding has\nidentically zero connected three-body cumulant. Deriving `f` therefore cannot\nclose the 3-body gap, because `f` is not what the gap is about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.isPairwise_ofBondFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.isPairwise_ofBondFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L177-L184","doc":"**Every bond-functional assembly is pairwise-additive**, for every `f`. This\nis the step that makes the Cauchy determination of `f` irrelevant to the 3-body\ndefect: `f` does not appear in the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.ofBondFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.ofBondFunctional","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L169-L175","doc":"The §10a assembly: a bond functional `f` evaluated on each bond factor `μ`\nand summed over the bonds of each cluster. `f` is entirely arbitrary — it is\n*not* assumed to be a logarithm, or continuous, or anything else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.not_isPairwise_of_b3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.not_isPairwise_of_b3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L161-L167","doc":"**The falsifiable form**, and the one the measurement instantiates: a binding\nmap with any nonzero connected three-body cumulant is not pairwise-additive.\nSince AME2020 gives `b₃ = +1.426222 ≠ 0`, the physical binding is not of this\nshape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b4_eq_zero_of_isPairwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b4_eq_zero_of_isPairwise","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L152-L159","doc":"**And vanishing connected four-body cumulant.** The `b₄` term inherits the\nresult: with every triple cumulant zero, `b₄` collapses to `quad - pairSum`,\nwhich pairwise-additivity sets to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3_eq_zero_of_isPairwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3_eq_zero_of_isPairwise","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L146-L150","doc":"**A pairwise-additive binding has vanishing connected three-body cumulant.**\nNot \"small\" — identically zero, for every triple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.IsPairwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.IsPairwise","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L135-L140","doc":"`M` is **pairwise-additive**: every cluster's binding is the sum of the pair\nbindings it contains. This is the shape §10a's assembly produces — the bond\nfunctional `f` is applied per bond and the results are summed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.b4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.b4","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L131-L133","doc":"The **connected four-body cumulant**: the whole-cluster binding, less the\npair terms and the connected triple terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.b3Sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.b3Sum","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L127-L129","doc":"The sum of the four triple cumulants of the four-body cluster. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.pairSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.pairSum","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L123-L125","doc":"The sum of the six pair bindings of the four-body cluster. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.b3","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L67-L121","doc":"The **connected three-body cumulant** of a triple: its binding, less the\nthree pair bindings inside it. This is the Ursell/Möbius definition, and it is\nthe quantity the AME inversion measures as `b₃ = +1.426222` MeV.\n\n**That figure is the ISOSPIN AVERAGE of the two A = 3 nuclei — say so when you\nquote it (provenance recorded 2026-08-30).** With the uniform pair value\n`e₂ = B(²H) = 2.224566`:\n\n* `b₃(³H)  = 8.481798 − 3e₂ = 1.808100`\n* `b₃(³He) = 7.718058 − 3e₂ = 1.044360`\n* mean **`= 1.426230`**, matching the quoted `1.426222` to `8·10⁻⁶` MeV — the\n  residual is AME input precision (it implies `B(²H) = 2.2245687` against\n  `2.2245660`, a 2.7 eV difference). Each single-nucleus alternative is **26.8 %\n  away**, so the identification is not a coincidence.\n\nWhy the average is the right object *here*: this file's binding model carries one\nuniform pair value, with no `pp`/`pn`/`nn` distinction — the regime\n`ChainBondOrderDependence.orderIndependent_iff` identifies as the physical one.\nThe entire ³H–³He splitting (`0.763740` MeV, dominantly the Coulomb repulsion of\n³He's second proton) therefore has nowhere to live but `b₃`, and averaging is what\nkeeps it from being charged to one nucleus.\n\n**Do not compare it directly against a triton-pinned `e₃`.** The body-order tower\npins `e₃ = (B(³H) − 3e₂)/M₃(³H) = 1.808100` on the triton *alone*, because that is\nthe nucleus whose single triple is genuinely Borromean (`lk = 0`, `μ̄₁₂₃ = +1`).\nThe two numbers differ by 27 % for that reason and not because either is wrong;\nthey are different conventions for the same order.\n\n**No theorem here depends on which convention is used**: `not_isPairwise_of_b3_ne_zero`\nneeds only `b₃ ≠ 0`, and `1.426222` and `1.808100` are both nonzero.\n\n**Prior art — this re-derives a result the corpus already held.** Bean `qou-9v7t`\n(2026-08-29, PR #5990, `computations/b3-charge-decomposition-a3.witness.json`)\nhad already split the A = 3 doublet into its charge-symmetric and\ncharge-antisymmetric parts and named them: `b3_sym = 1.4262225` — *\"the strong\nchannel's obligation\"*, the figure above — against `b3_asym = 0.3818775`, half\nthe mirror splitting, *\"the EM channel's\"*. The identification here is that\nresult reached again from the other end; it is recorded because the **docstring**\ncarried the number without it, not because the number was unknown.\n\n**One question that bean leaves open, and this docstring should not paper over.**\nThe symmetric/antisymmetric split is exact bookkeeping, but it is *not* the same\nas a Coulomb correction: ³H has a single proton and so no `pp` pair at all, while\n³He has one. So the Coulomb energy is not charge-antisymmetric about the mean —\nremoving it moves the **mean**, not only the difference, and it moves it toward\nthe triton value. Whether the strong-channel obligation is `1.426` or nearer\n`1.81` is therefore a live 27 % question on the very quantity the magnitude gate\nis short by 6–14×, and the bean's own \"live successor\" note says the EM channel\nat A = 3 is unaddressed. External precedent points the same way: Platter, Hammer\nand Meißner fix their **SU(4)-symmetric** three-nucleon parameter from\n`B(³H) = 8.48` MeV — the triton alone (`platter2005tjon`, and\n`mba-remark-tjon-universality-external`). Nothing here settles it; it is flagged\nso the average is not read as adjudicated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.quad","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L61-L61","doc":"the binding of the whole four-body cluster — an independent datum ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.triple","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L59-L59","doc":"the binding of the triple `{i, j, k}` — an independent datum ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.pair","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L57-L57","doc":"the binding of the pair `{i, j}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.BindingMap","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairwiseCumulantVanishing.lean#L52-L61","doc":"A binding map on a four-body system, recorded by its values on every\nsub-cluster **independently**. Nothing here assumes the values are related;\n`IsPairwise` below is what asserts a relation, and it is a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}